Here is the refactored `UserService` with constructor injection:

```typescript
interface Database {
  query<T>(sql: string, params?: unknown[]): Promise<T | null>;
}

class UserService {
  constructor(private readonly db: Database) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<User | null> {
    return this.db.query<User>(
      'SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE id = $1',
      [id]
    );
  }

  async create(data: Omit<User, 'id'>): Promise<User> {
    const result = await this.db.query<User>(
      'INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING *',
      [data.name, data.email]
    );
    if (!result) { throw new Error('Insert returned no row'); }
    return result;
  }
}
```

In tests, pass a mock that implements the `Database` interface.

With structured error handling and logging:

```typescript
import { Logger } from './logger';

class UserService {
  constructor(
    private readonly db: Database,
    private readonly logger: Logger
  ) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<User | null> {
    try {
      this.logger.debug('findById', { id });
      const user = await this.db.query<User>(
        'SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE id = $1',
        [id]
      );
      return user;
    } catch (err) {
      this.logger.error('findById failed', { id, err });
      throw new Error(
        `Failed to fetch user ${id}: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`
      );
    }
  }
}
```

The most common causes of stale state in React:

**1. Mutating state directly (most common)**
```jsx
// ❌ Wrong — mutates existing object, React sees same reference
state.items.push(newItem);
setState(state);

// ✅ Correct — new array reference triggers re-render
setState(prev => ({ ...prev, items: [...prev.items, newItem] }));
```

**2. Stale closure in event handler**
```jsx
// ❌ Wrong — onClick captures stale `count`
useEffect(() => {
  document.addEventListener('click', () => setCount(count + 1));
}, []);

// ✅ Correct — functional update always uses latest state
document.addEventListener('click', () => setCount(c => c + 1));
```

**3. Object identity in dependency array**
```jsx
// ❌ New object on every render → infinite loop
const opts = { debounce: 300 };
useEffect(() => { /* ... */ }, [opts]);

// ✅ Memoize or move outside the component
const opts = useMemo(() => ({ debounce: 300 }), []);
```
